-- title:
--   Diamond operators on the function field of X_H(q²M')
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L((\mathsf q))$ over $L$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb Q \to L$ of the $\mathbb Q$-subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H)` of $\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$, where $H$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ and [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $(q^2M')$ $H$ is the image in $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) sending $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(q^2M')$ to its lower right entry as a unit mod $q^2M'$. The assertion is the existence of a group homomorphism $\rho : \Gamma_0(q^2M') \to (K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[L]} K)$ with four properties. First, a transport rule for $q$-expansions: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(q^2M')$, every weight $k \in \mathbb Z$, all modular forms $f, g, f_1, g_1$ of weight $k$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $(q^2M')$ $H$ regarded as a subgroup of $GL(2,\mathbb R)$, all power series $p_f, p_g, p_{f_1}, p_{g_1} \in \mathbb Z[[X]]$ and every nonzero $c \in \mathbb C$, if each of the four series maps under $\mathbb Z \to \mathbb C$ to the width-one $q$-expansion of the corresponding form, if $f_1 = c\,(f \mid_k \gamma)$ and $g_1 = c\,(g \mid_k \gamma)$ as functions on the upper half plane (with $\gamma$ viewed in $GL(2,\mathbb R)$), and if the Laurent series `intSeriesC L` of $p_g$ and of $p_{g_1}$ are nonzero, then for every $x \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is `intSeriesC L` $p_f$ divided by `intSeriesC L` $p_g$, the Laurent series of $\rho(\gamma) x$ is `intSeriesC L` $p_{f_1}$ divided by `intSeriesC L` $p_{g_1}$. Second, each $\rho(\gamma)$ fixes every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series lies in the $L$-base change of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (q ^ 2 * M')`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), the $\mathbb Q$-subfield generated by the expansions of $j$ at the divisors of $q^2M'$. Third, conversely, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ fixing that subfield pointwise is of the form $\rho(\gamma)$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(q^2M')$. Fourth, $\rho(\gamma) = 1$ if and only if [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units (q ^ 2 * M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) $\gamma$ lies in the subgroup generated by $H$ together with $-1$ in $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$.
--
--   This identifies the diamond operators as the full automorphism group of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ over that of $X_0(q^2M')$, after base change to an arbitrary field $L$ of characteristic zero, together with the rule by which they act on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms and the description of their kernel as the subgroup of units congruent to $\pm 1$ modulo $q$. It is used in the construction of charts and coefficient conditions on the full-level curve at $q^2M'$.
